resources/presets/Quicksave2/
# forgejo#88: `resources/presets/test/` (directory-slash form) ignored the
# WHOLE directory, and git will not descend into an ignored directory to
# apply a file-level negation below it -- FFTMAG.milk/GETFFT.milk were
# silently never committable, not merely never written, until this changed
# to the `/*` (contents-glob) form specifically so they could be carved out.
# The rest of the folder is still RUNTIME scratch (ad-hoc debug presets
# dropped there during a session -- see the "test_preset_location"
# convention); FFTMAG.milk/GETFFT.milk are deliberate, committed fixtures
# that happen to live in the same folder because the folder is also what
# gets a presets.json exemption (AnnotationIgnoreDirs) -- purpose-built
# probe shaders TestFFTProfileApplied/TestShaderUniforms load by exact path,
# not something any run generates.
resources/presets/test/*
!resources/presets/TEST/FFTMAG.milk
!resources/presets/TEST/GETFFT.milk
settings.ini
settings.ini.bak
messages.ini
messages.ini.bak
src/settings.ini
src/messages.ini
.worktrees/

tools/comparison/

# Preset files are never repository content.
#
# resources/presets/ is a WORKING directory -- it is where the running app puts
# imports, where a Shader Import lands, and where anything being tried out
# accumulates. Twenty-five .milk3 files were tracked here, and twelve of them
# arrived in one `git add -A` during a directory reorganisation (153b9bde) that
# nobody meant to include them in. Several were conversions of other people's
# published GLSL Sandbox and Shadertoy shaders.
#
# release.ps1 already refuses to bundle this directory for exactly that reason
# ("licences are not ours to redistribute") -- but the repository is published
# too, so keeping them out of the ZIP was only half the rule.
#
# The engine needs no preset to be present: it comes up on the one compiled
# into the exe (builtin_preset.h) and asks the user to point it at a library.
*.milk
*.milk2
*.milk3

# ...except the two purpose-built probe presets, which are this project's own
# and are loaded BY EXACT PATH by test_audio_profiles. They were exempted at
# lines 66-67 above; a blanket rule added later overrides an earlier negation,
# so the exemption has to be restated here rather than left up there.
!resources/presets/TEST/FFTMAG.milk
!resources/presets/TEST/GETFFT.milk

# ...and except bundle/, which is the OPPOSITE of resources/presets.
#
# Nothing writes to bundle/ at runtime -- it is not a working directory, it is
# the demo set that ships in the ZIP, and every file in it was chosen against
# stated criteria rather than swept up by a `git add -A`:
#
#   * .milk only. A .milk3 is a converted GLSL shader and carries its author's
#     terms; one in this tree states them outright ("You cannot host, display,
#     distribute or share this Work neither as is or altered").
#   * no port of an individual shader artist's published work, even where the
#     port is a .milk -- same concern, different extension.
#   * no third-party texture. Every preset here needs either no image at all or
#     only the randNN slots, which bundle/textures fills.
#   * classic MilkDrop lineage: authors whose presets have shipped inside
#     MilkDrop, projectM and BeatDrop distributions for about twenty years.
#
# See bundle/CREDITS.md. Add nothing here that has not been through that list.
!bundle/presets/*.milk


# MD3 PRO-derived shaders are personal-use only: recovered from a local licensed
# install by tools/md3_shader_import.py, and never redistributable. Keep them
# under a recovered/ directory so they cannot be committed by accident.
resources/shaders/recovered/
*.recovered.hlsl

# Python bytecode
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Lexer unit-test build output
tools/lexer-test/bin/

# npm dependencies are regenerable from package.json + package-lock.json and do
# not belong in history. They were tracked here for a long time: 3,487 of the
# repo's 3,984 files -- 88% of it -- while package.json itself was untracked.
node_modules/

# Editor and assistant working dirs, and loose captures that accumulate at the
# repo root during display/preset testing. Ignored rather than deleted -- they
# are working files, just not repository content.
.grok/
.kilo/
.vscode/launch.json
/d1_*.png
/d2_*.png
/d3_*.png
/port_view_*.jpg

# Everything private, in one place and never in git.
#
# tools/ (the probe harness and MCP server), mcps/, the agent working notes
# under docs/superpowers and docs/plans, and the local push-guard hooks all
# moved here. Previously they were tracked and stripped at publish time by a
# nine-path list duplicated between sync-public.yml and the pre-push hook,
# which had to be kept in step by hand.
#
# CLAUDE.md, .claude/ and .mcp.json cannot move: Claude Code discovers them at
# the repo root, and the memory junction points into .claude/memory. They stay
# tracked and stay on the publish strip list.
private/

# Claude Code writes per-machine permission rules here as they are granted.
# .claude/ is only PARTLY ignored -- memory/project/ is tracked deliberately --
# so without this line a file full of one machine's absolute paths would be
# committable, in a repo whose Forgejo remote force-push-mirrors to GitHub.
.claude/settings.local.json
